Version 1.0
-----------
	o First Release

Version 1.1
-----------
	o oopss.. kept forgetting to keep this file updated ;)
	o Fixed some annoying install bugs for Martin.
	o Fixed (hopefully) a few Enforcer hits (naughty, nasty!)
	o Mail Processor :
		o Now scans INBOUND: for #?.pkt's #?.mo|tu|etc? packets
		  and unpacks, and imports them.
		o Export not working as yet, but this is something to
		  be getting on with.
	o Archivers :
		o Config Re-written... now has Recog Sturf working.
		o {f} & {s} flags changed to ~a + ~f.
	o Few REXX Bug-Fixes
	o NEW PLMSGCFG->Systems... For configuring systems you feed
	  from PLMP. Fairly straight-forward...
	o I lost the include file, so a few structures *may* have changed.
	  If you are experiencing strangeness with the configuration
	  files, delete and start again.
	o New Function in 'readmsg.pl' for backwards message reading.
	o What else? Oh, a few more pipeutil.library functions.
	o General Cleanup....
	o Unreleased.

Version 1.2 (Beta 2)
-----------

	o Added New REXX Function 'ListMsgAreas'. Pretty basic lister for
	  message areas, as previous 'un wasn't fast enough. If you want
	  this jazzed up with ansi codes + the like, write me a message
	  on how you would like the REXX Function worked (args etc.).
	o Added InitMsgScanKey(),
		CloseMsgScanKey(),
		ScanMessages() to pipeutil.library.
	o NB: Some routines are still unimplemented in the pipeutil.library.
	  Check out 'include:clib/pipeutil_protos.h' to see what are
	  written. (protos are only done for implemented funcs.)
	o Fixed REXX Function GetPointer.
	o Released to Alex for Distribution
		(Please See Problems with ScanMsgs.Pl!)
	o Waiting Mail

Version 1.3 (Beta 3)
-----------

	o New library function (GetPointers())
	o Added EXPORT to MAIL PROCESSOR!
	o Made SaveMessage() support waiting mail.
	o Fixed problems with logging on on remote lines.
	o Still 2 'forcer hits.
	o PLMSGCFG -
		o Redid FidoAddresses.

Version 1.4 (Beta 4)
-----------

	o Fixed double freemem in CloseConfig ().
	o All enforcer hits disappeared.
	o PLMSGCFG	
		o Fixed bug with USE without Sel. (loses Fido Address)
	o Geez! It was a triple freemem. Gone...

	o put all Mail:#? files in Mail:PlMail/#?
	o Fixed bug in InitMsgScanKey()

Version 1.5 (Beta 7)
-----------

	o Fixed some bugs in PLMP
	o Added GetThread Rexx Command.
	o Fixed bug in WriteMsg
	o Re-wrote pipeline:scripts/readmsgs.pl
	o Tidy-up of REXX Functions.
	o Added new Gadget in PLMSGCFG
	o Fixed some PLMSGCFG-related bugs.
	o Added Linkage Code to SAVEUSER, so that Editor and Current Area
		information will be saved out to disk.                                                                        
	o Added GETEDITOR and CHANGEEDITOR Rexx Commands.
	o Fixed some stoopid bugs.
	o Fixed RC bug in CHANGEMSGAREA
	o Fixed bug in WriteMsg()->MakeEditorString() with Ed Stack Size.
	o Re-wrote Gui in MsgStats for larger message area names.
	o Implemented IDCMP_CLOSEWINDOW.
	o Added ProgramLog() func to pipeutil.library.
	o Added log writing for PLMSG
	o Added Optional screen logging to PLMSG

Version 1.6 (Beta 8)
-----------

	o Weeel... I managed to send the above version out, but it was't
	  very special was it? I forgot to add the new scripts for
	  your delectation...
	o New READMSG.PL (with Original/Thread/Reply/Help working)
	o New WAITINGMAIL.PL (which works ;))
	o Alpha-sorting in Files!!! (Forwards/Backwards)

Version 1.7 (beta 9)
-----------
	BaudRates - Doesn't close the pipeline.library or the pipeutil.library
	Archivers - Doesn't close the pipeline.library or the pipeutil.library
	PlMsgCfg  - Doesn't close the pipeline.library or the pipeutil.library
	FIXED

	PLMsgCfg/
	- If traplist.library isn't present it complains but runs but gurus when
	     defining fido addresses.
	FIXED

	PLMsgCfg/Message Areas/
	- If you select a base, modify and then 'Use'.  Clicking on 'Edit' has no
	     effect even though the name is still in the string gadget.
	FIXED

	PLMsgCfg/Message Areas/
	- Can you not quit out when you save the data.
	INDEED I DO NOW!

	PLMsgCfg/Networking/FidoNet Addresses/
	- When selecting an address, activate the string gadget.
	DONE
	- When entering a new address, can you get the password from
	     traplist.library if it's been defined.
	DONE

	Bugs:
	- Doesn't quit if you've been doing anything with messages.
	Found to be a problem in LoadMsg. FIXED

	PLMsgCfg/Networking/FidoNet Systems/
	- When selecting an address, activate the string gadget.
	DONE

	Editors   - Doesn't close the pipeline.library or the pipeutil.library
	FIXED

	Minor Changes:
	- When you save, don't quit.
	DONE

	o Won't crash if PLMSG is already running, and you try to
	  load it.
	o Added New Flag in PLMSGCFG, PVT UUCP BASE.
	o Got rid of RebuildMessages() library function. Re-compile
	  all programs which use pipeutil.library
	o Recompiled the lot for new version of Pipeline (180294)
	o Changed MAIL: assigns to Config->Paths->Mail
	o NODELIST-Config->Paths->Mail ignored!
	o All config files are referenced from Pipeline:Config/
	o Some interesting new Pipeutil.library functions
		- ReadAddresses()
		- WriteAddresses()
		- FreeAddresses()
		- CompareAddresses()
	o New usage for PLMSG :

		PLMSG [LOG]

			Log - Make the log file appear on the screen, as
				well as in the written log file. Useful
				for debugging.
	o Due to the new Paths configuration, I do not store the mail
	   files in MAIL:PlMail/ anymore, but simply in the directory
	   specified by Config->Paths->Mail. Please copy all data files
	   across, as appropriate.

Version 1.8 (beta 20)
-----------

	o Added Mail Packet type selector to PlMsgCfg->Networking->Systems
		You can choose between Type-1 (FTS-1 rev 12.), Type 2 
		(derivative of FSC-38 & 45), and Type-2.2 (FSC-48) to
		Export.
	o Re-wrote a lost module of PLMP (scan.c), using ExAll() to
		scan inbound files.
	o Cheerz Ross for some useful Packet handling routines which are
		being slapped into PLMP.
	o Bevelled up PlMsgCfg->Networking->Systems. Looks spesh!
	o Made the AreasModified code much smarter in PlMsgCfg->Areas.
	o Fixed nasty bug in PLMSG which meant that the MAIL:MsgText.n
		files would be re-initialised every time PLMSG was run!

Version 1.9 (beta 21)
-----------

	o Fixed broken Import in PLMP. The problem was that the message
		new-line characters were getting all stripped and stropped!
		The LineWrap() pipeutil.library routine was crashing on
		it and stuff like that. All very boring, but rest assured
		the PLMP Import should be very good now.
	o Made quoted lines change colour!
	o Fixed ProgramLog () so no enforcer hits.
	o Fixed SaveMessage() enforcer hits.

Version (beta 27)
-----------------

	o Cleaned up, and ANSI-ed up some scripts.
	o Re-wrote callSysop program. Looks alot better, have a look
		at the callsysop.lha archive.
	o Waiting Mail File now IS written.
	o Writemsg.pl improved
	o filelist.pl improved
	o changeprotocol.pl improved
	o MsgEditor jazzed up, and made alot better.
	o GetMsgAreaFlag now working.
	o CallSysop now works from Remote
	o PlMsgCfg->Area->EditArea ghosts appropriate Gadgets depending
		on which Basetype is set.
	o WriteMsg.pl now supports Private Mail.
	o MsgEditor clever ANSI routines removed, when they were
		discovered not to be that clever ;)
	o Netmail Routing Gui designed (but not implemented).

Version (beta 29/30)

	o Editors GUI fixed when Pipeline not running.
	o LastCallers Door Written.
	o User High Message Pointers stored and used.
	o New ControlCodes %2030-%2050 (see PlMsgCC.Doc)
	o Written some rather special new scripts which control Logon
		Stack. See PostLogon.pl ReadLogonCfg.pl and CfgLogon.pl
	o Templates GUI program for User Access Templates.
	o New USEREDITOR program.
	o New Messages Working
	o PlMp - added some more techie stuff ;)

Version 0.101
	o Message Editor now puts AREA:TAGNAME line at start of FidoNet areas.
	o PLMP now imports the AREA:%TAGNAME line into Pipeline.
	o PLMP now creates FLO files with a '-' prefix, which causes Trapdoor
to send out files and delete with logging.
	o SaveMessage now creates default tagline with '\r' suffix.
	o SaveMessage now makes sure that From/To lines are never more than
	36 characters, and Subject lines never above 72. May have caused
	INMP crashes.
	o Fixed bug in Plmp which put it in an endless loop in Import.
	o ListMsgAreas now truncates the Area Name to 30 characters, so
	it looks alright on screen.
	o ChangeSig Rexx Command (links with PlFile one).
	o ListMsgAreas IGNORESIG
	o ChangeMsgArea ALL. See PlFile->history.doc for details.

Version 0.102
	o DeleteMessage() and EditMessage() routines/docs written for
	pipeutil.library
	o Fixed bug in EditFile().
	o Changed mainmenu.src/changesig.pl scripts to remove the SetVar
	statements, and use CallScript instead.
	o Fixed some non-Close() file-handle bugs in LoadMessage().
	o Changed PrintMsgHdr to print out line by line, with More
	(YES/no) prompt if reaches end of line. If the user wishes
	the output to end, then PrintMsgHdr returns 5.
	o Changed scanmsg.pl script to support above.
	o MsgEditor now logs each Message Written.
	o SigEditor doesn't crash if Pipeline isn't running.
	o SigEditor now unlocks the public screen, so Control can quit.
	o Problem fixed with PlMp importing crash.
	o Now updating $VER: tag in PlMsg.
	o New buttons in SigEditor -
		AddAll -- Add's all the Message/File areas.
		DelAll -- Delete's all the currently selected Message/File
		areas.
	o New Script in Pipeline:Bin called PlVersion. Basically goes
		through EVERY pipeline program looking at the VER string.
		And, it seems, most don't have one. Perhaps one should
		be put in, the output from the script will be a useful
		function for solving bugs...
	o Renamed PrintMsgText, DisplayMsg. Please change all your scripts
		accordingly.
	o Now saves SIG selection.
	o Fixed problem with OpenTextFile() / LoadMsg.

Version 0.103
-------------
	o Updated $VER:
	o Fixed the quoting system in MsgEditor to something a little more
		refined ;)
	o Fixed a few naughties in MsgEditor, re: LineWrapping.
	o Fixed bug in DlgConvFileCfg. Works now!
	o Will not create AREA: line if not Echomail/UUCP base.
	o New PLFILE/PLMSG Usage...
		PLFILE/MSG LOG/S,SCR=SCREENLOG/S
          Log -- Write log to disk.
          Scr -- Write log to screen.
        o In my opinion, you can't trust the Optimise feature in SAS/C
           for hello.c, ne'ermind PLMP, so PLMP is now non-optimised,
           and alot healthier for it.
	o Fixed some more PLMP stuff.
	o MsgEditor Quoting now looking better.
	o SaveMessage no longer creates Origin and Tagline strings
	   in message areas which do not require them.
	o Improved script readmsg.src/.pl
	o MsgEditor no longer saves all messages as Private.
	o ChangeMsgArea now returns the previous message area number
	   in result, if the area is changed successfully.
	o Leave Feedback to Sysop in the mainmenu and the logoff
	   scripts now changes the area to 1 - Feedback to Sysop,
	   and back to the previous area.
	o Fixed readmsg.src/.pl high message pointer handling, so
	   that it isn't one off any more.
	o No longer displays AREA: line.
	o Fixed nasty in MsgEditor.
	o Fixed bug in PlMsgCfg->Network->Addresses with CloseWindow.
	o PLMP now deletes packets in t:
	o Checkboxes in PlMsgCfg->Areas updating properly.
	o DisplayMsg now realises that a \r is a real character ;).
	o New Conversion Utilty - XenoMsgConv for converting Xeno
	   1.90 Msg.Config files into Pipeline Format.
	o UserEditor: Replaced Reqtools File Requester with my own
	   Listview gadget for aesthetics sake.
	o Finally fixed some niggling bugs in MsgEditor.
	o MsgEditor quoting now ends with '\r', should solve Al's
	   reflow problems.
	o ChangeMsgArea now returns 2 if the user's access level is
	   not high enough, and ListMsgAreas will not display the name
	   of an area the user does not have access to.
	o Fixed a possible memory conflict bug.
	o Rewrote DisplayMsg. It was getting a bit dumb.

Version 0.104
-------------

	o Sped up PLMSG by stopping it scanning every message file on
	startup. People were complaining of load times of up to 2 and
	a half minutes. Should be much faster now.
	o Important note: CallSysop is now a PLDoor.
	o Finally fixed that dumb problem with the Quoting in MsgEditor.
	o Two new Rexx Functions. SetMsgFilter and DeleteMsgFilter.
	Used for Message Searching and Reading Messages using the 
	FROM/TO/SUBJECT lines as filters. See plmsgrexx.guide.
	o New Script SearchMsgMenu.pl
	o New Script ReadMsgMenu.pl
	o Changed scripts for use with new filtering functions, msgmenu.pl
	readmsg.pl.
	o Found quite a few nasty bugs re: the Message Indexing Funcs.
	o GetNumberOfMessages() should now be fine.
	o Combed through source looking for possible mem overflows,
	mem errors, and eliminated a few. Should make PlMsg more stable.
	o SaveMessage() now saves the correct TextLength.
	o Fixed error in SetMsgFilter.
	o Made PlMp in Import mode faster.
	o Hopefully fixed MsgEditor line-wrap bug.

Version 0.105
-------------

	o Forgot to send updated CallSysop out with last release!
	o Re-done Line Wrap (sometimes wouldn't wrap) in MsgEditor.
	o Due to problems with SAS C 6.50, gone back to SAS C 6.3 to 
          compile Pipeline with, and as such, all programs updated.

Version 0.106
-------------

	o Combed through most of the PLMSG and PLFILE code with a
